# The kernel work of 2026-09-20. Each patch is measured in tools/htp-lab against a
# float64 reference, in the cycle-accurate simulator, and its header carries the
# cycles and the error before and after.
#
# THREE OF THEM GIVE A WRONG MODEL ON THE DEVICE AND THE LAB DOES NOT SEE IT.
# On 2026-09-20 the NPU answered every prompt with one repeated token, while the
# CPU and the GPU were correct. A bisect of the series on the phone, one variant
# for each prefix, isolated 0004 and 0011. The other twelve patches of that day
# are good. 0010 is out because it needs the context that 0004 gives to
# unary-ops.c, and because it wires the same int16 activation tables that 0011
# selects. Refer to the header of each patch.
#
# Why the lab passed them: it measures one kernel that it compiles on its own,
# with a token count that is a multiple of 4 vectors, against a float64
# reference. The library compiles the same source with -flto into a translation
# unit of a different shape, and the model calls it with ne0 = the head count.
# A lab result is thus necessary and not sufficient: every kernel patch needs
# one generation on the device before it goes into this file.

